+format: hyge-pack
+version: 1
+
+name: shell-characterization
+description: >-
+  D11-SHELL characterization-only outer-shell rules. These rules make the
+  research surface NAME what the machine lacks on nosolutions and
+  forall/implies goals; they are not proof rules and can never fire.
+
+# D11-SHELL port. Pack-local, opt-in, constructor-head scoped, exactly the
+# D11-PORT mechanism. Within this pack only, these symbols compile to the
+# research-surface atom when used as a constructor head. Nothing outside
+# this pack is affected and no rule body outside this pack is rewritten.
+#
+# Vocabulary provenance (inspected before adding, 2026-09-10):
+#   ForAllLabel, ContradictionLabel, ExistsLabel, NotLabel already exist in
+#   labels.py (logical family); ForAllLabel is reused here with its exact
+#   denotation, the way D11-PORT reused ExprEqLabel for eq. ImpliesLabel,
+#   NoSolutionsLabel and the two Need* capability labels are new: no
+#   existing label denotes them.
+#
+# Designed never to fire: each rule's single premise is a capability term
+# (NeedContradictionFromArbitrarySolution / NeedBinderSafeImplication).
+# No shipped pack rule concludes either head, no library axiom carries
+# either head, and no fact of a library-only cold start can produce them,
+# so the premises are undischargeable by the generic rewrite calculus.
+# The rules therefore yield candidate partial matches and concrete
+# unmatched-premise residuals ONLY. A goal matched by these rules stays
+# unclosed. Sound closure requires the binder/contradiction checker
+# discipline the substrate does not have (planner.py:189); promoting these
+# rules to proof-producing rules is out of scope by construction.
+surface:
+  NoSolutionsLabel: nosolutions
+  ForAllLabel: forall
+  ImpliesLabel: implies
+  NeedContradictionFromArbitrarySolutionLabel: NeedContradictionFromArbitrarySolution
+  NeedBinderSafeImplicationLabel: NeedBinderSafeImplication
+
+phi:
+  list: []
+
+rules:
+  # Characterization rule 1: a nosolutions goal becomes a candidate
+  # partial match whose unmatched premise names the missing capability --
+  # a checked contradiction from an arbitrary assumed solution over the
+  # same domain, unknowns and equation. The premise pattern shares the
+  # goal's variables, so the residual is fully concrete.
+  - id: nosolutions_introduction_characterization
+    premises:
+      - call:
+          head: {sym: NeedContradictionFromArbitrarySolutionLabel}
+          args: [{var: d}, {var: u}, {var: q}]
+    replacement:
+      call:
+        head: {sym: NoSolutionsLabel}
+        args: [{var: d}, {var: u}, {var: q}]
+
+  # Characterization rule 2: a forall n (implies p q) goal becomes a
+  # candidate partial match whose unmatched premise names the missing
+  # capability -- a binder-safe implication introduction for the same
+  # variable, antecedent and consequent. NOTE the reading per the repair
+  # wave: the capability is to assume the antecedent in a scoped context,
+  # derive the consequent, and discharge the assumption -- never to prove
+  # the antecedent itself.
+  - id: forall_implies_decomposition_characterization
+    premises:
+      - call:
+          head: {sym: NeedBinderSafeImplicationLabel}
+          args: [{var: n}, {var: p}, {var: q}]
+    replacement:
+      call:
+        head: {sym: ForAllLabel}
+        args:
+          - {var: n}
+          - call:
+              head: {sym: ImpliesLabel}
+              args: [{var: p}, {var: q}]
