@@ -0,0 +1,158 @@
+# D11-SHELL — characterization-only outer-shell rules
+
+The D11-SHELL-ENG repair-wave ticket (Agent 2). Phase 1 (this lane,
+ratified at `b55d66e`) established the frontier: bare `eq` matches, the
+`nosolutions` and `forall`/`implies` shells are silent, and the blocker
+for sound closure is the checker's missing binder discipline
+(`planner.py:189`). This is the characterization half: the machine must
+NAME what it lacks on those shells. It is not proof support.
+
+```text
+pack:         packs/shell-characterization.pack.yaml
+surface map:  NoSolutionsLabel -> nosolutions
+              ForAllLabel -> forall
+              ImpliesLabel -> implies
+              NeedContradictionFromArbitrarySolutionLabel ->
+                  NeedContradictionFromArbitrarySolution
+              NeedBinderSafeImplicationLabel ->
+                  NeedBinderSafeImplication
+              (constructor heads only; pack-local, opt-in)
+rules:        2, both single-premise, both designed never to fire
+probes:       Goal A  (nosolutions positive-integers (unknowns x)
+                        (eq (plus x 1) x))            non-FLT
+              Goal B  (forall n (implies (greater n 1)
+                        (eq (plus a a) (plus a a))))  non-FLT
+matches:      A: before 0, after 1, ablation 0
+              B: before 0, after 1, ablation 0
+```
+
+## Acceptance sentence, met
+
+> Goal A and Goal B, previously silent (0 genuine partial matches,
+> zero-successor-root residual) under library-only cold start, each get
+> >= 1 genuine partial match with a concrete unmatched premise naming the
+> missing checker capability, remain unclosed, and return to 0 when the
+> shell rules are disabled; a shell goal with a different head symbol
+> stays at 0 throughout.
+
+## Numbers
+
+| run | state | cost | partials | residual |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| A before | `bfd4bd2`, no shell pack | 334 | **0** | zero-successor-root |
+| A after | shell pack shipped | 338 | **1** | missing `(NeedContradictionFromArbitrarySolution positive-integers (unknowns x) (eq (plus x 1) x))` |
+| A ablation | committed tree, pack's `surface:` header stripped | 338 | **0** | zero-successor-root |
+| B before | `bfd4bd2`, no shell pack | 334 | **0** | zero-successor-root |
+| B after | shell pack shipped | 338 | **1** | missing `(NeedBinderSafeImplication n (greater n 1) (eq (plus a a) (plus a a)))` |
+| B ablation | committed tree, pack's `surface:` header stripped | 338 | **0** | zero-successor-root |
+
+Negative controls (both states, shipped): an `implies`-headed goal and
+an `over`-wrapped goal — head symbols no shipped rule concludes — stay
+at 0 partials with zero-successor-root. An arity-only variation would
+not count: head compatibility is compared by value, so the control
+differs in head symbol.
+
+Fresh process and cold boot each time; one worktree per state. Logs:
+`verification/probes/2026-09-10-shell-phase2/`. Ablation is the D11-PORT
+mechanism: the pack's `surface:` header stripped, so its rules still
+compile (169 library rules) but with label heads that match nothing --
+the rules are present and disabled, not deleted. The gate's S1/S5 prove
+the same silence with the pack excluded from the load path entirely.
+
+## The two rules
+
+```text
+nosolutions_introduction_characterization
+  premises     NeedContradictionFromArbitrarySolution(?d ?u ?q)
+  conclusion   nosolutions(?d ?u ?q)
+
+forall_implies_decomposition_characterization
+  premises     NeedBinderSafeImplication(?n ?p ?q)
+  conclusion   forall(?n implies(?p ?q))
+```
+
+Reading (per the repair-wave brief): the nosolutions capability is a
+checked contradiction from an arbitrary assumed in-domain solution; the
+forall/implies capability is to assume the antecedent in a scoped
+context, derive the consequent, and discharge the assumption — never to
+prove the antecedent itself.
+
+## Designed never to fire
+
+Each rule's single premise is a capability term. No shipped pack rule
+concludes either capability head, no library axiom carries either head,
+and no fact of a library-only cold start can produce them, so the
+premises are undischargeable by the generic rewrite calculus. The gate
+proves it mechanically (S6): probing each capability term as a goal
+finds zero candidate rules anywhere in the shipped packs. The rules
+therefore produce candidate partial matches and concrete residuals only;
+a matched goal stays unclosed. Promoting either rule to a
+proof-producing rule requires the binder/contradiction checker
+discipline the substrate does not have (`planner.py:189`) and is out of
+scope by construction.
+
+## Vocabulary provenance (inspected before adding)
+
+Existing: `ForAllLabel`, `ContradictionLabel`, `ExistsLabel`, `NotLabel`
+(the logical family, `labels.py`), plus `NeedLabel` (dependency
+requests) and `FreshenedLabel`/`BinderLabel` (the planner's side
+conditions). `ForAllLabel` is reused here with its exact denotation, the
+way D11-PORT reused `ExprEqLabel` for `eq`. New: `ImpliesLabel` and
+`NoSolutionsLabel` (the missing members of the logical family's surface
+spelling) and the two `Need*` capability labels — no existing label
+denotes them. `NeedLabel` itself was NOT reused for the capability
+premises: it is the dependency-request term, and overloading it would
+make a capability residual indistinguishable from a theorem request.
+
+## Scope held
+
+```text
+shipped:       shell-characterization only (1 new pack, 2 rules, 5 labels)
+not ported:    the other 13 packs — reference digests byte-identical
+rewritten:     no existing rule body; only a new pack + PACK_PATHS entry
+search:        untouched
+matcher:       untouched
+checker:       untouched (no rewrite calculus change, no weakening)
+planner:       untouched
+parser:        untouched (the shells already parsed; they were silent)
+arithmetic:    ExprEqLabel -> eq port untouched (gate P1/P2 unchanged)
+machine-wide:  none; the mapping is pack-local and opt-in
+FLT words:     zero occurrences of fermat/flt/wiles/frey/pow/times/
+               exponent/minus/divides/solutionmap in the shell pack (gate S7)
+```
+
+`nosolutions` appears in the shell pack as the generic logical
+constructor the repair wave itself names (the toy goals and the parser
+use it); it is not FLT vocabulary. The FLT-specific words are banned
+outright by S7, and the arithmetic port's stricter P4 scan (which bans
+`nosolutions` for THAT port) is unchanged.
+
+## Baselines
+
+The `surface:`-stripped reference state moved from 167 to 169 compiled
+rules (the two new rules compile with label heads when their header is
+stripped). `protocol/d11-spike/shipped-rules.sha256` (renamed from
+`shipped-167-rules.sha256`) records count 169 and the reference digest;
+`shipped-pack-digests.txt` gains exactly one line (the shell pack's
+no-headers compilation); the 13 pre-shell reference lines are
+byte-identical. Shipped-state digests of `arithmetic` and
+`shell-characterization` drift from the reference by design (gate
+condition 1 expects exactly that drift and no other).
+
+## Gate
+
+`tools/d11_gate.py` extended with S1–S8 (see its docstring): shell pack
+absent -> silence; Goal A/B -> >=1 partial, concrete capability premise,
+attributed, unclosed; controls -> 0; ablation -> silence; capability
+goals -> 0 (never fires); vocabulary scan; surface-audit provenance.
+16/16 conditions pass on the committed tree; full output at
+`verification/2026-09-10-d11-shell-gate-16of16.txt`.
+
+## Explicitly not claimed
+
+No quantified proof support. No forall-introduction, implication-
+introduction, or refutation checking. The rules expose child obligations
+as concrete unmatched premises; sound closure of the shells is
+LOGIC-CHECKER-ENG's ticket (Agent 3) and must not ride through these
+rules. A mapped head is not shell support: only the checker-validated
+calculus would be.
